WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.660
Let's look at how to add negative keywords to a campaign that's already running.

00:00:04.180 --> 00:00:08.848
Say you're advertising a premium product, and you don't want your ad to appear when customers use

00:00:08.848 --> 00:00:11.320
queries like cheap, because these aren't relevant for customers.

00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:13.513
Find your campaign or ad group.

00:00:13.513 --> 00:00:16.740
In the menu on the left, you'll find the negative targeting option.

00:00:17.320 --> 00:00:19.760
From here, click on the button to add negative keywords.

00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:24.240
Enter your negative keywords, set the match type, add them, and click Save.

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:28.760
Now your ad won't appear when shopper search terms match your negative keywords.
